problem:
Problem description
- There are $$P$$ finished products indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, $$R$$ raw materials indexed by $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$, optional limited-capacity resources indexed by $$k \in \mathcal{K}$$, and planning periods indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- Each product $$p$$ has a unit selling price $$s_{p,t}$$, a unit variable processing cost $$v_{p,t}$$, and a recipe that specifies the amount $$a_{r,p}$$ of each raw material $$r$$ needed per unit produced.
- Each raw material $$r$$ has a unit purchase cost $$q_{r,t}$$ and a period-specific purchase limit $$U_{r,t}$$.
- Each restricted resource $$k$$ has a period-specific capacity $$C_{k,t}$$, and each product $$p$$ may consume a known amount $$b_{k,p}$$ of that resource per unit produced.
- Market demand may be finite or effectively unlimited, represented by $$D_{p,t}$$, and the department may sell any quantity it produces as long as market demand and production availability permit it.
- The planning goal is to choose production and purchasing decisions so that total profit over $$\mathcal{T}$$ is maximized, which also maximizes the manager’s salary if salary is profit-based.
- Business requirements:
  - raw material purchases in each period must respect the available purchase limits;
  - product output must be supported by the available purchased raw materials according to each product’s recipe;
  - any restricted machine or facility capacity must not be exceeded in any period;
  - sales cannot exceed what is produced and cannot exceed market demand if a demand limit is provided;
  - all decision quantities must remain nonnegative.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: quantity of product $$p$$ produced in period $$t$$.
  - $$y_{p,t}$$: quantity of product $$p$$ sold in period $$t$$.
  - $$u_{r,t}$$: quantity of raw material $$r$$ purchased in period $$t$$.
  - $$\Pi$$: total profit over the planning horizon.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Number of periods in $$\\mathcal{T}$$, with periods indexed by $$t \\in \\mathcal{T}$$."
  },
  "products": {
    "type": "array",
    "description": "List of products indexed by $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$."
  },
  "resources": {
    "type": "array",
    "description": "List of raw materials indexed by $$r \\in \\mathcal{R}$$."
  },
  "restricted_resources": {
    "type": "array",
    "description": "List of limited-capacity resources or machines indexed by $$k \\in \\mathcal{K}$$."
  },
  "selling_price": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$s_{p,t}$$ is the unit selling price of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$."
  },
  "material_requirements": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{P}|$$",
    "description": "$$a_{r,p}$$ is the amount of raw material $$r$$ required per unit of product $$p$$."
  },
  "purchase_cost": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$q_{r,t}$$ is the unit purchase cost of raw material $$r$$ in period $$t$$."
  },
  "production_cost": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$v_{p,t}$$ is the unit variable processing cost of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$."
  },
  "purchase_limit": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$U_{r,t}$$ is the maximum amount of raw material $$r$$ that can be purchased in period $$t$$."
  },
  "resource_usage": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{K}| \\times |\\mathcal{P}|$$",
    "description": "$$b_{k,p}$$ is the amount of restricted resource $$k$$ consumed by one unit of product $$p$$."
  },
  "resource_capacity": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{K}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$C_{k,t}$$ is the available capacity of restricted resource $$k$$ in period $$t$$."
  },
  "demand_limit": {
    "type": "matrix or infinite indicator",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$D_{p,t}$$ is the maximum sellable quantity of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$; if demand is unlimited, use $$+\\infty$$ or omit this field."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "total_profit": {
    "type": "number",
    "description": "The optimal value of $$\\Pi$$."
  },
  "production_plan": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$x_{p,t}$$, the quantity of each product to produce in each period."
  },
  "sales_plan": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$y_{p,t}$$, the quantity of each product to sell in each period."
  },
  "purchase_plan": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "description": "$$u_{r,t}$$, the quantity of each raw material to purchase in each period."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "planning_horizon": "$$1$$",
  "products": ["Meaties", "Yummies"],
  "resources": ["Grains", "Meat"],
  "restricted_resources": ["Meaties machine"],
  "selling_price": [["$$2.80$$"], ["$$2.00$$"]],
  "material_requirements": [
    ["$$2.0$$", "$$3.0$$"],
    ["$$3.0$$", "$$1.5$$"]
  ],
  "purchase_cost": [["$$0.20$$"], ["$$0.50$$"]],
  "production_cost": [["$$0.25$$"], ["$$0.20$$"]],
  "purchase_limit": [["$$400000$$"], ["$$300000$$"]],
  "resource_usage": [["$$1$$", "$$0$$"]],
  "resource_capacity": [["$$90000$$"]],
  "demand_limit": [["$$+\\infty$$"], ["$$+\\infty$$"]]
}
